# STLport 5.2.1 — our SEMANTIC delta from pristine upstream.
#
# Upstream: https://sourceforge.net/projects/stlport/files/STLport/STLport-5.2.1/STLport-5.2.1.tar.bz2
#           sha256 755b007b982c4545086c43affc8ed32c0acd577ee206eb1f6967e250c3546fc9
# Apply from vendor/stlport/ for the a/... paths, and from
# sdk/include/c++/stlport/ for the a/stlport/... paths (see SPLIT TREE below).
#
# Version 5.2.1, from sdk/include/c++/stlport/stl/_stlport_version.h
# (_STLPORT_MAJOR 5 / _STLPORT_MINOR 2 / _STLPORT_PATCHLEVEL 1 / _STLPORT_VERSION 0x521),
# corroborated by etc/ChangeLog's last entry, 2008-12-10 "STLport release 5.2.1".
# The README's "STLport 5.0" is simply stale — do not believe it. 5.2.1 is the FINAL
# STLport release ever made, so "bump to the latest" is already satisfied and there is
# no upstream left to track.
#
# SPLIT TREE — this caught us out, and vendor.yaml did not record it:
#   vendor/stlport                src/, build/, doc/, etc/, test/  (the library sources)
#   sdk/include/c++/stlport       326 files = upstream's top-level stlport/ include tree
# The second directory was NOT registered in vendor.yaml at all until 2026-09-20. It is
# not a copy of the first; it is the other half of the same drop.
#
# *** DELIBERATELY NOT A COMPLETE PATCH ***
# 50 further files differ ONLY by CRLF / trailing whitespace (37 in the lib half, 13 in
# the include half). They carry zero semantic content and including them would bury the
# 30 real changes in thousands of lines of line-ending noise, so they are excluded.
# Consequence: pristine + this patch does NOT reproduce the tree byte-for-byte. Verify
# the claim yourself with:
#     diff <(sed -e 's/\r$//' -e 's/[[:space:]]*$//' A) <(sed -e 's/\r$//' -e 's/[[:space:]]*$//' B)
#
# WE CARRY TWO GENUINE UPSTREAM BUG FIXES. Re-vendoring naively would REGRESS both:
#   src/locale.cpp:211   upstream: strcmp(name1, name1) == 0     <- compares to ITSELF
#                        ours:     strcmp(name1, name2) == 0
#                        Upstream's always-true test defeats the locale-name equality
#                        check documented directly above it.
#   stlport/stl/_fstream.c:87  upstream: __ok == __ok && this->_M_unshift();
#                              ours:     __ok =  __ok && this->_M_unshift();
#                        Upstream wrote == where = was meant, so the result — including
#                        the _M_unshift() outcome — is computed and thrown away. Note
#                        upstream gets it RIGHT at line 710 of the same file.
#
# THE ONE ARCHITECTURAL CHANGE: the fstream backend is switched from native Win32 I/O to
# C stdio, by three coordinated edits — host.h uncomments _STLP_USE_STDIO_IO, _windows.h
# wraps its `#define _STLP_USE_WIN32_IO` in `#if 0`, and host.h also uncomments
# _STLP_USE_STATIC_LIB. src/fstream.cpp's #elif chain then compiles
# details/fstream_stdio.cpp instead of fstream_win32io.cpp (the latter is vendored but
# dead). Matching additions carry it: fstream_stdio.cpp gains a 35-line
# _Filebuf_base::_M_open(FILE*, openmode) that upstream lacks, and _fstream.h gains the
# declarations, guarded by `#if defined (_STLP_USE_STDIO_IO)`. This is a CRT-interop
# addition, not a macro toggle, so it cannot be reduced to a -D.
#
# OTHER REAL CHANGES worth knowing about:
#   stl/config/_reactos.h    NEW FILE (added by this patch). A compiler-config header in
#                            STLport's standard style, "Copyright 2010 Jerome Gardou",
#                            dispatched from stl/config/_system.h under #if __REACTOS__.
#   stl/_limits.h            #undef min/max (windef.h pollution) and drops upstream's
#                            defensive (_STLP_CALL min)() parenthesisation.
#   stl/_num_put.c           adds an explicit `#ifdef _WIN64 // ReactOS, compilation with
#                            64 bit gcc` branch — LLP64 correctness, and one of the few
#                            hunks in the whole tree that names ReactOS.
#   stl/_vector.h            adds C++11 data(); STLport 5.2.1 predates it.
#   stl/_cstdlib.h           uncomments the long long abs() overload.
#   src/stdio_streambuf.cpp  ORs __REACTOS__ into the condition selecting plain
#                            fseek/fsetpos over _fseeki64.
#   stl/config/user_config.h activates _STLP_NEW_PLATFORM_SDK,
#                            _STLP_USING_PLATFORM_SDK_COMPILER, _STLP_DONT_USE_AUTO_LINK.
#                            These are presence-only macros with no structural coupling —
#                            the ONE cluster here that really could move into the build as
#                            target_compile_definitions. Worth doing; left alone in this
#                            pass because it changes the build, not just the record.
#   stl/config/features.h    adds _M_ARM64 to the arch-detection #elif chain. Needed by
#                            this project's whole reason for existing.
#   stddef.h, stl/_cprolog.h, stl/config/compat.h, stl/config/features.h
#                            wrap their bodies in #ifndef RC_INVOKED so the resource
#                            compiler can include them transitively. Build shim.
#   src/dll_main.cpp         DROPS upstream's #define _STLP_EXPOSE_GLOBALS_IMPLEMENTATION.
#                            Probably inert — features.h forces it to 1 whenever
#                            __BUILDING_STLPORT is set — but not exhaustively proven, so
#                            treat as ambiguous rather than as known-dead.
#
# ODDITY, flagged not fixed: stlport/errno.h has a stray `#define errno foo` that the
# 5.2.1 tarball does not. It sits immediately before an `#error`, so it can never take
# effect. It looks like an example from the comment above it that leaked out of the
# comment. Harmless, but it means our copy is not a strict subset of the tagged release —
# consistent with the two bug fixes above, i.e. this tree may have been synced from a
# post-tag SVN revision rather than from the tarball.
#
